   "desc": "Chicago AI, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup **Date, Time and Location** Nov 09, 2026 9:00 AM - 10:00 AM PST Online. **[Register for the Zoom!](https://voxel51.com/events/when-prompting-beats-training-agentic-labeling-for-specialized-visual-data-november-9-2026)** Frontier multimodal models handle familiar concepts well and struggle on niche ones: sorting drill-core samples into 35 geological classes, or telling adhesion from scarring on a ceramic substrate. Our study across 11 specialized visual datasets in manufacturing inspection, geology, and medical imaging found that a few labeled examples in the prompt can close much of that gap, and it also found where that stops working. **What you’ll learn:** * Niche versus hard: how in-context examples supply domain knowledge a model is missing, and how to tell a niche task from a genuinely hard one * What the study measured: on an industrial defect task, one labeled example per class raised macro-F1 from 34% to 59% with no fine-tuning, while on other tasks trained specialists pulled ahead at 5 to 10 examples per class * Building a few-shot labeling task: define classes, pick reference examples, preview predictions on a small batch, and refine the instructions * Finding the crossover point: when to stop prompting a foundation model and train a specialist on bootstrapped labels * Running it on your own data: attendees get free GPU compute from Nebius to try the workflow after the session",
