   "desc": "AWS Chicago User Group ### Get Hands on with Claude Code, featuring AWS DA Lucas Swanson In this hands-on workshop, you will learn how to accelerate team development and scale Claude Code deployments on Amazon Bedrock. * configure team environments * establish standards and workflows * maximize Claude Code's capabilities * learn advanced deployment patterns for Claude agents using the Agent SDK on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Runtime. **Suitable for:** This workshop is designed for developers, engineering leaders, technical leads, and DevOps professionals from small to large teams looking to learn Claude Code concepts to improve productivity and scale and/or roll out Claude Code to their team. **Level:** 300 (Advanced). No background knowledge necessary, however familiarity with Typescript or Python and AWS services will be useful. **Duration:** We expect the workshop to take approximately **3 hours** to complete. **Prep:** bring your laptop to participate. To streamline the workshop sign in, [sign up for AWS builder center](https://builder.aws.com/) and review the [steps of the workshop here. ](https://catalog.workshops.aws/claude-code-on-amazon-bedrock/en-US/getting-started/3-setup-aws)[ ](https://builder.aws.com/) **Getting there:** We will be in room 0807 in the Loyola University Schreiber Center building, between State and Pearson St. Enter on Pearson Street. Take the CTA Red Line! (Chicago Station, 25 East Pearson Street) nearby [parking](https://www.luc.edu/campustransportation/generalinformation/watertowercampus/) garages include: One West Superior Standard Parking Fordham Garage 900 N Michigan Self-Park NEW: you can also see events and register on AWS Builder Center: https://builder.aws.com/connect/event/ae1e77e4-cbe7-3559-9b3b-2fb75cefe64d",
